<urn:atm:triage:finding/FTQ-017>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "FTQ-017" ;
  triage:title "heartbeat_demotes_evicted_member_to_explicit_unknown uses IsoTimestamp::now() tight loop — min_by_key nondeterministic on timestamp ties (tests.rs:501)" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/tests.rs:501 — heartbeat_demotes_evicted_member_to_explicit_unknown inserts 4097 members via IsoTimestamp::now() tight loop. min_by_key at runtime_health.rs:242 over HashMap is nondeterministic on timestamp ties when the loop runs faster than clock resolution. Fix: use synthetic monotonically-increasing timestamps in the insertion loop. Similar to FTQ-012 which was fixed in TASK-1148 on S.2; verify whether the S.2 merge-forward at 9698a17 already resolved this occurrence. (quality-mgr reported as FTQ-002 in S.3 QA-2 report.)" ;
  triage:category "FTQ" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
